    "category": "Surg Cardio",
    "q": "What is the mechanism of bilateral pitting edema from right heart failure?",
    "a": "Right heart failure decreases the ability to fill the right heart, raising central venous pressure and systemic venous hydrostatic pressure, so fluid transudates from systemic veins and venules into the interstitium of the legs.",
